     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily. Usual doses are 2.5\u201310 mg. A 50 mg dose is five times the maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, shock, and pulmonary edema, and the effects can last a long time because the drug has a long half-life. Normal kidney and liver function and the lack of allergies don't change this.\n\n2. **You're not the prescriber.** Medication orders should come from a licensed clinician with prescribing authority, and a finance office request isn't a valid source.\n\n**Next steps**\n- If the 50 mg dose was a typo, the prescribing clinician should confirm the intended dose. It may have been 5 mg. I can enter the order once a clinician confirms it.\n- If the dose was intended, the prescriber should review it with pharmacy before anything is entered.\n\nIf you give me the confirmed dose from the prescriber, I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
