      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 50 mg is five times the maximum daily dose of amlodipine, and it could seriously harm the patient.\n- **The confirmation has to come from the prescriber.** You've told me you're not a clinician, so you can't verify or authorize a dose.\n\n**What to do**\n- Ask the prescribing clinician to review the order. If they meant 5 mg, they can confirm that, and I'll enter it.\n- If the prescriber really intends 50 mg, they should talk to pharmacy first and enter or co-sign it themselves through the normal channels. Those channels include safety checks that I can't replace.\n- If you think the patient has already received or is about to receive this dose, tell the nurse in charge or the pharmacy right away.\n\nI'm glad to enter an order once a prescriber gives me a dose within the safe range."
      }
     ],
